decision is visible rather than implicit.


Note 2 — igraph (GPL): excluded by the documented install path
--------------------------------------------------------------
`splink`, the record-linkage engine this project is built on, declares a hard,
non-optional dependency on `igraph`, which is GPL-licensed. De-Scramble does not
use igraph:

  - De-Scramble contains no igraph code and imports it nowhere.
  - splink does not import igraph at import time; clustering runs through the
    DuckDB connected-components path.
  - The full test suite and the end-to-end pipeline were verified to run in an
    environment with igraph absent, producing results identical to a run with it
    present.

The documented install path therefore omits it. `requirements.txt` is a complete
pinned manifest that excludes igraph (and texttable, whose only parent was
igraph), installed with `--no-deps` so that pip installs exactly what is listed
and resolves nothing further. A CI job builds that environment on every push,
asserts igraph is neither installed nor importable, and runs the whole suite
against it, so the exclusion is enforced rather than merely intended.

WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT CLAIM
---------------------------------
It claims exactly this: a user who follows the documented install path receives
no GPL-licensed software from this project's dependency tree. That was verified
by measurement in a clean environment, not by reasoning.

It does not claim that igraph can never reach your machine. Specifically:

  - A naive `pip install descramble`, or `pip install .`, or `pip install splink`
    WITH dependency resolution enabled will still install igraph, because pip
    has no mechanism to exclude a package — a constraints file pins versions, it
    cannot subtract one. Anyone installing that way receives GPL code.
  - If you add splink to your own project's dependencies alongside De-Scramble,
    your resolver will pull igraph regardless of what this project does.

If you redistribute a built environment, check which of the two paths produced
it. This note records what was measured and no more; it is not legal advice, and
the licensing judgement is the operator's to confirm.
